@* Data for reaction rates.

% $Id$

% $Log$
% Revision 1.6  1995/08/09 18:00:02  dstotler
% Define a set of arrays analogous to the main "reaction_data" arrays
% called reaction_misc which hold miscellaneous data.
%
% Revision 1.5  1995/06/12 13:07:13  karney
% Add in dummy elements into common blocks to avoid complaints from
% Alpha.
%
% Revision 1.4  1995/04/25 22:14:47  karney
% Initial version of sources.web
%
% Revision 1.3  1995/04/24 20:43:43  karney
% Generalize reactiondata to allow multiple data arrays per reaction.
%
% Revision 1.2  1995/04/24 14:21:25  karney
% Remove some unused variables.  Introduce a coordinate system for plasma
% flow.
%
% Revision 1.1  1995/01/30 21:06:50  karney
% Merge in my changes with Daren's
%

\ID{$Id$}

Data for reactions is held in arrays in common blocks.
|rd_datan(x,m,...)| accesses the data for the $m$th table as an $n$d array.
Miscellaneous (i.e., not cross section or reaction rate) data is handled
in the analogous |rd_misc_data3| array.

@m rd_data1(x,m,i) reaction_data_table[reaction_data_base[x][m]+i]
@m rd_data2(x,m,i,j) reaction_data_table[reaction_data_base[x][m]+i+reaction_data_tab_index[x][m][1]*j]
@m rd_data3(x,m,i,j,k) reaction_data_table[reaction_data_base[x][m]+i+reaction_data_tab_index[x][m][1]*(j+reaction_data_tab_index[x][m][2]*k)]

@m rd_rate1(x,i) rd_data1(n,rd_rate,i)
@m rd_rate2(x,i,j) rd_data2(n,rd_rate,i,j)
@m rd_rate3(x,i,j,k) rd_data3(n,rd_rate,i,j,k)

@m rd_xs1(x,i) rd_data1(n,rd_xs,i)
@m rd_xs2(x,i,j) rd_data2(n,rd_xs,i,j)
@m rd_xs3(x,i,j,k) rd_data3(n,rd_xs,i,j,k)

@m rd_xs 1
@m rd_rate 2

@m rd_misc_data3(x,m,i,j,k) reaction_misc_table[reaction_misc_base[x][m]+i+reaction_misc_tab_index[x][m][1]*(j+reaction_misc_tab_index[x][m][2]*k)]

